# Memory update on new articles

When you **add or edit** site content under:

- `aileena-new/app/blog/**` (articles)
- `aileena-new/app/updates/**`
- `aileena-new/lib/research/**`

## Auto (preferred)

Merging to **`main`** triggers GitHub Action **Machina Memory (Dreaming)**
(`.github/workflows/machina-memory.yml` path filter). It runs:

`pnpm sync:content-memory` → `pnpm dreaming` → `pnpm build:memory-index` → commits L3 memory.

You do **not** need to ask the user to “start dreaming” after a normal article merge.

## Local / before merge (optional)

```bash
cd aileena-new && pnpm memory:on-article
# alias of memory:workflow
```

Commit the resulting `aileena_second_brain/memories/**` changes in the same PR if you want memory live before CI, or leave it to the post-merge Action.

## Do not

- Manually edit `latest-content.md` by hand — regenerate via sync.
- Expect chat to know a brand-new article until sync/Dreaming has run (or Vercel rebuilds with the committed memory files).
